// `invert`: the pin's level is the opposite of the value. The program sees
// the value -- an active-low relay is on at 1 like any other -- and only the
// board layer drives and reads the level. On the host there is no pin, so the
// value is all there is; what this holds is that the option is read, kept and
// listed, and that an inverted pulled-up input rests at 0 (its level high).
#digital Rel  out invert 11
#digital Btn  in pullup invert 4
#digital Plain in pullup 5
#variable On:1 = 1
#variable SeenBtn:1 = 1
#variable SeenPlain:1 = 0
#variable SeenRel:1 = 0
Rel = On
SeenBtn = Btn
SeenPlain = Plain
SeenRel = Rel
